Two versions, the original here in (D) and also in (G) mainly for fingerstyle.

TIP:  There's a (D) in front of and an (A) after the word "gold".  Don't linger on the (A).  Play it and get ready for the next (D) and begin the chorus.

TIP:  An (A) will follow the (A6) so either play the (A6) with four fingers and lift the pinky off the first string, or play as a 4-string barre and lift the bottom pad of your index finger up and off the bottom string.


